[
  {"id":"ohms_law","title":"Ohm's law","text":"Drag the voltage or resistance slider and watch the current (the ammeter, and how fast the dots move) follow I = V / R. Voltage across the resistor always equals the source.","analysis":"dc","sliders":[{"part":"V1","prop":"V","min":0,"max":20,"label":"Voltage"},{"part":"R1","prop":"R","min":100,"max":10000,"log":1,"label":"Resistance"}],"dmm":{"a":[4,0],"b":[4,4]},"parts":[{"type":"V","x":0,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"V":10},"name":"V1"},{"type":"AM","x":0,"y":0,"p":{},"name":"A1"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"R1"},{"type":"VM","x":8,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{},"name":"VM1"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":4,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[4,0,8,0],[8,4,0,4]]},
  {"id":"series_parallel","title":"Series and parallel resistors","text":"R2 and R3 are in parallel (1 k total) in series with R1 and R4: total 3 k, so 4 mA flows. The two parallel branches split it evenly (2 mA each). Change R3 and watch the split change.","analysis":"dc","sliders":[{"part":"R3","prop":"R","min":500,"max":8000,"log":1,"label":"R3"}],"dmm":{"a":[4,0],"b":[4,4]},"parts":[{"type":"V","x":0,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"V":12},"name":"V1"},{"type":"R","x":0,"y":0,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"R1"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":2000},"name":"R2"},{"type":"R","x":8,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":2000},"name":"R3"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":4,"rot":2,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"R4"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":4,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[4,0,8,0],[4,4,8,4]]},
  {"id":"voltage_divider","title":"Voltage divider","text":"Vout = Vin * R2 / (R1 + R2) = 7.5 V here. Slide R2 and the output voltage (colour of the tap wire and the voltmeter) follows; the same current flows through both resistors.","analysis":"dc","sliders":[{"part":"R2","prop":"R","min":100,"max":10000,"log":1,"label":"R2"},{"part":"V1","prop":"V","min":0,"max":20,"label":"Vin"}],"dmm":{"a":[8,4],"b":[8,8]},"parts":[{"type":"V","x":0,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"V":10},"name":"V1"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"R1"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":4,"rot":1,"p":{"R":3000},"name":"R2"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":8,"name":"GND"},{"type":"VM","x":8,"y":4,"rot":1,"p":{},"name":"VM1"}],"wires":[[0,0,4,0],[0,4,0,8],[4,8,0,8],[4,4,8,4],[8,8,4,8]]},
  {"id":"current_divider","title":"Current divider","text":"A 10 mA source splits between two parallel branches in inverse proportion to their resistance: the smaller resistor takes the larger share (7.5 mA vs 2.5 mA). Change R2 and watch the ammeters.","analysis":"dc","sliders":[{"part":"R2","prop":"R","min":500,"max":10000,"log":1,"label":"R2"}],"parts":[{"type":"I","x":0,"y":4,"rot":3,"p":{"I":0.01},"name":"I1"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":8,"name":"GND"},{"type":"AM","x":4,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{},"name":"A1"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":4,"rot":1,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"R1"},{"type":"AM","x":8,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{},"name":"A2"},{"type":"R","x":8,"y":4,"rot":1,"p":{"R":3000},"name":"R2"}],"wires":[[0,4,0,8],[0,0,8,0],[0,8,8,8]]},
  {"id":"kvl_kcl","title":"Kirchhoff's laws","text":"KVL: voltages around any loop sum to zero. KCL: currents into node A (4 mA) equal currents out (3 mA down R2 + 1 mA into V2). Hover wires and parts to read V and I, then check the sums.","analysis":"dc","explainNode":[4,0],"sliders":[{"part":"V2","prop":"V","min":0,"max":15,"label":"V2"}],"parts":[{"type":"V","x":0,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"V":10},"name":"V1"},{"type":"R","x":0,"y":0,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"R1"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":2000},"name":"R2"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":0,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"R3"},{"type":"V","x":8,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"V":5},"name":"V2"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":4,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[0,4,8,4]]},
  {"id":"nodal_analysis","title":"Nodal analysis","text":"Write KCL at nodes A and B and solve: A = 7.6 V, B = 6.4 V. The simulator did exactly that (that is what MNA is). Change the current source and re-check the node equations.","analysis":"dc","explainNode":[8,0],"sliders":[{"part":"I1","prop":"I","min":0,"max":0.004,"label":"I source"}],"parts":[{"type":"V","x":0,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"V":12},"name":"V1"},{"type":"R","x":0,"y":0,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"R1"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":2000},"name":"R3"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":0,"p":{"R":2000},"name":"R2"},{"type":"R","x":8,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":4000},"name":"R4"},{"type":"I","x":12,"y":4,"rot":3,"p":{"I":0.001},"name":"I1"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":4,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[8,0,12,0],[0,4,12,4]]},
  {"id":"superposition","title":"Superposition","text":"In a linear circuit each source contributes independently: V(A) = 0.5*V1 + 0.25*V2. Set V2 to 0 (it becomes a short), note V(A); set V1 to 0 and note it again; the sum equals V(A) with both on.","analysis":"dc","explainNode":[4,0],"sliders":[{"part":"V1","prop":"V","min":0,"max":20,"label":"V1"},{"part":"V2","prop":"V","min":0,"max":20,"label":"V2"}],"parts":[{"type":"V","x":0,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"V":10},"name":"V1"},{"type":"R","x":0,"y":0,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"R1"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":2000},"name":"R2"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":0,"p":{"R":2000},"name":"R3"},{"type":"V","x":8,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"V":8},"name":"V2"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":4,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[0,4,8,4]]},
  {"id":"thevenin","title":"Thevenin equivalent","text":"Any linear network seen from two terminals looks like one source Vth in series with Rth. Open \"What's happening?\": it computes Vth = 8 V and Rth = 1.17 k seen from A-B, and predicts the load voltage you see on the RL slider.","analysis":"dc","thev":{"a":[8,0],"b":[8,4]},"sliders":[{"part":"RL","prop":"R","min":100,"max":20000,"log":1,"label":"Load RL"}],"parts":[{"type":"V","x":0,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"V":12},"name":"V1"},{"type":"R","x":0,"y":0,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"R1"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":2000},"name":"R2"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":0,"p":{"R":500},"name":"R3"},{"type":"R","x":8,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":1500},"name":"RL"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":4,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[0,4,8,4]]},
  {"id":"max_power","title":"Maximum power transfer","text":"A source with 1 k internal resistance feeds a lamp. The lamp glows brightest (25 mW) when its resistance equals the source resistance. Slide RL below and above 1 k and watch it dim.","analysis":"dc","thev":{"a":[4,0],"b":[4,4]},"sliders":[{"part":"RL","prop":"R","min":100,"max":10000,"log":1,"label":"Lamp RL"}],"parts":[{"type":"V","x":0,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"V":10},"name":"V1"},{"type":"R","x":0,"y":0,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"Rs"},{"type":"LAMP","x":4,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":2500,"Pr":0.025},"name":"RL"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":4,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[0,4,4,4]]},
  {"id":"rc_charging","title":"RC charging","text":"A square wave charges the capacitor through R: it reaches 63.2% of the step after one time constant tau = RC = 10 ms, and is essentially full after 5 tau. Change R or C to stretch or squeeze the curve.","analysis":"tran","scope":{"tdiv":0.01,"v1":2,"v2":2,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[0,0]},{"ch":2,"at":[4,0]}],"sliders":[{"part":"R1","prop":"R","min":200,"max":5000,"log":1,"label":"R"},{"part":"C1","prop":"C","min":0.000001,"max":0.000047,"log":1,"label":"C"}],"parts":[{"type":"VP","x":0,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"lo":0,"hi":5,"f":10,"duty":0.5,"td":0.01},"name":"V1"},{"type":"R","x":0,"y":0,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"R1"},{"type":"C","x":4,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"C":0.00001},"name":"C1"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":4,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[0,4,4,4]]},
  {"id":"rl_transient","title":"RL transient","text":"An inductor resists sudden changes in current: the voltage across it jumps to the full step and decays with tau = L/R = 1 ms as the current builds up. Probe 2 is the inductor voltage.","analysis":"tran","scope":{"tdiv":0.002,"v1":1,"v2":1,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[0,0]},{"ch":2,"at":[4,0]}],"sliders":[{"part":"L1","prop":"L","min":0.02,"max":0.5,"log":1,"label":"L"}],"parts":[{"type":"VP","x":0,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"lo":0,"hi":5,"f":50,"duty":0.5,"td":0.002},"name":"V1"},{"type":"R","x":0,"y":0,"p":{"R":100},"name":"R1"},{"type":"L","x":4,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"L":0.1},"name":"L1"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":4,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[0,4,4,4]]},
  {"id":"rlc_damping","title":"RLC damping","text":"A series RLC rings after each step. Slide R: below 63 ohm (zeta < 1) it is under-damped and rings, near 63 ohm it is critically damped, above it over-damped and sluggish. Probe 2 is the capacitor voltage.","analysis":"tran","scope":{"tdiv":0.0015,"v1":1,"v2":1,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[0,0]},{"ch":2,"at":[8,0]}],"tran":{"uic":true},"sliders":[{"part":"R1","prop":"R","min":5,"max":300,"log":1,"label":"R (ohm)"}],"parts":[{"type":"VP","x":0,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"lo":0,"hi":1,"f":50,"duty":0.5,"td":0.002},"name":"V1"},{"type":"R","x":0,"y":0,"p":{"R":20},"name":"R1"},{"type":"L","x":4,"y":0,"p":{"L":0.01},"name":"L1"},{"type":"C","x":8,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"C":0.00001},"name":"C1"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":4,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[0,4,8,4]]},
  {"id":"ac_phasors","title":"AC phasors: R and L","text":"In an inductor the current lags the voltage. Here XL = R, so the current (the voltage across R, probe 2) lags the source by 45 degrees and has 0.71 of the maximum amplitude. Change the frequency to move the phase from 0 to 90 degrees.","analysis":"tran","scope":{"tdiv":0.0002,"v1":5,"v2":5,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[0,0]},{"ch":2,"at":[4,0]}],"bode":{"in":[0,0],"out":[4,0],"fmin":10,"fmax":100000},"sliders":[{"part":"V1","prop":"f","min":100,"max":10000,"log":1,"label":"Frequency"}],"parts":[{"type":"VAC","x":0,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"A":5,"f":1000,"ph":0,"off":0},"name":"V1"},{"type":"L","x":0,"y":0,"p":{"L":0.16},"name":"L1"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"R1"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":4,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[0,4,4,4]]},
  {"id":"power_factor","title":"Power factor correction","text":"An inductive load draws current that lags the voltage (power factor about 0.8). Click the switch to add a 25 uF capacitor in parallel: the current comes back in phase with the voltage and the line current drops. Probe 2 is the line current (drop across a 2 ohm sense resistor).","analysis":"tran","scope":{"tdiv":0.003,"v1":5,"v2":0.2,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[0,0]},{"ch":2,"at":[0,0],"ref":[4,0]}],"sliders":[],"parts":[{"type":"VAC","x":0,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"A":10,"f":60,"ph":0,"off":0},"name":"V1"},{"type":"R","x":0,"y":0,"p":{"R":2},"name":"Rs"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":8,"name":"GND"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":50},"name":"Rload"},{"type":"L","x":4,"y":4,"rot":1,"p":{"L":0.1},"name":"Lload"},{"type":"SW","x":8,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"on":0},"name":"S1"},{"type":"C","x":8,"y":4,"rot":1,"p":{"C":0.000025},"name":"C1"}],"wires":[[0,4,0,8],[4,0,8,0],[0,8,8,8]]},
  {"id":"low_pass","title":"RC low-pass filter","text":"Low frequencies pass, high frequencies are attenuated. The corner frequency is fc = 1/(2 pi R C) = 1 kHz: there the gain is -3 dB and the phase -45 degrees. Open the Bode tab, then slide the source frequency in the scope.","analysis":"ac","scope":{"tdiv":0.0002,"v1":1,"v2":1,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[0,0]},{"ch":2,"at":[4,0]}],"bode":{"in":[0,0],"out":[4,0],"fmin":10,"fmax":100000},"sliders":[{"part":"C1","prop":"C","min":2e-8,"max":0.000001,"log":1,"label":"C"}],"parts":[{"type":"VAC","x":0,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"A":1,"f":1000,"ph":0,"off":0},"name":"V1"},{"type":"R","x":0,"y":0,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"R1"},{"type":"C","x":4,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"C":1.5915e-7},"name":"C1"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":4,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[0,4,4,4]]},
  {"id":"high_pass","title":"RC high-pass filter","text":"Now the capacitor is in series and the resistor to ground: low frequencies are blocked, high frequencies pass. Same corner fc = 1 kHz (-3 dB, +45 degrees).","analysis":"ac","scope":{"tdiv":0.0002,"v1":1,"v2":1,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[0,0]},{"ch":2,"at":[4,0]}],"bode":{"in":[0,0],"out":[4,0],"fmin":10,"fmax":100000},"sliders":[{"part":"R1","prop":"R","min":200,"max":10000,"log":1,"label":"R"}],"parts":[{"type":"VAC","x":0,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"A":1,"f":1000,"ph":0,"off":0},"name":"V1"},{"type":"C","x":0,"y":0,"p":{"C":1.5915e-7},"name":"C1"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"R1"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":4,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[0,4,4,4]]},
  {"id":"band_pass","title":"Series RLC band-pass","text":"Only frequencies near the resonance f0 = 1/(2 pi sqrt(LC)) = 503 Hz pass to the resistor. The smaller R, the narrower the band (higher Q). Look at the Bode plot while you slide R.","analysis":"ac","scope":{"tdiv":0.001,"v1":1,"v2":1,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[0,0]},{"ch":2,"at":[8,0]}],"bode":{"in":[0,0],"out":[8,0],"fmin":50,"fmax":5000},"sliders":[{"part":"R1","prop":"R","min":2,"max":200,"log":1,"label":"R (ohm)"}],"parts":[{"type":"VAC","x":0,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"A":1,"f":503,"ph":0,"off":0},"name":"V1"},{"type":"L","x":0,"y":0,"p":{"L":0.01},"name":"L1"},{"type":"C","x":4,"y":0,"p":{"C":0.00001},"name":"C1"},{"type":"R","x":8,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":10},"name":"R1"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":4,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[0,4,8,4]]},
  {"id":"notch","title":"Notch (band-stop) filter","text":"A series LC \"trap\" to ground shorts out its resonant frequency (503 Hz) so the signal is removed there, while other frequencies pass. See the deep dip in the Bode plot.","analysis":"ac","scope":{"tdiv":0.001,"v1":1,"v2":1,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[0,0]},{"ch":2,"at":[4,0]}],"bode":{"in":[0,0],"out":[4,0],"fmin":50,"fmax":5000},"sliders":[{"part":"C1","prop":"C","min":0.000003,"max":0.00003,"log":1,"label":"C"}],"parts":[{"type":"VAC","x":0,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"A":1,"f":503,"ph":0,"off":0},"name":"V1"},{"type":"R","x":0,"y":0,"p":{"R":100},"name":"R1"},{"type":"L","x":4,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"L":0.01},"name":"L1"},{"type":"C","x":4,"y":4,"rot":1,"p":{"C":0.00001},"name":"C1"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":8,"rot":1,"p":{"R":2},"name":"Rc"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":12,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[0,4,0,12],[0,12,4,12],[4,12,4,12],[4,12,4,12]]},
  {"id":"resonance_q","title":"Resonance and Q","text":"Voltage across the capacitor of a series RLC peaks near f0 = 503 Hz by a factor Q = sqrt(L/C)/R. Lower R and the peak grows taller and narrower. The Bode plot reports the peak and the -3 dB bandwidth.","analysis":"ac","scope":{"tdiv":0.001,"v1":1,"v2":5,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[0,0]},{"ch":2,"at":[8,0]}],"bode":{"in":[0,0],"out":[8,0],"fmin":100,"fmax":3000},"sliders":[{"part":"R1","prop":"R","min":1,"max":100,"log":1,"label":"R (ohm)"}],"parts":[{"type":"VAC","x":0,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"A":1,"f":503,"ph":0,"off":0},"name":"V1"},{"type":"R","x":0,"y":0,"p":{"R":10},"name":"R1"},{"type":"L","x":4,"y":0,"p":{"L":0.01},"name":"L1"},{"type":"C","x":8,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"C":0.00001},"name":"C1"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":4,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[0,4,8,4]]},
  {"id":"transformer","title":"Transformer","text":"Two magnetically coupled coils: the secondary voltage is the primary voltage times the turns ratio (here 2:1 step-down: the secondary has half as many turns) and the current goes the other way. Only a changing current couples through, so a steady DC input gives no steady secondary voltage.","analysis":"tran","scope":{"tdiv":0.002,"v1":5,"v2":5,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[0,0]},{"ch":2,"at":[4,0]}],"bode":{"in":[0,0],"out":[4,0],"fmin":5,"fmax":10000},"sliders":[{"part":"T1","prop":"n","min":0.1,"max":3,"log":1,"label":"Ns/Np"}],"parts":[{"type":"VAC","x":-4,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"A":10,"f":60,"ph":0,"off":0},"name":"V1"},{"type":"GND","x":-4,"y":4,"name":"GND"},{"type":"XF","x":0,"y":0,"p":{"L1":1,"n":0.5,"k":0.99},"name":"T1"},{"type":"R","x":8,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":50},"name":"RL"}],"wires":[[-4,0,0,0],[-4,4,4,4],[4,0,8,0],[4,4,8,4]]},
  {"id":"half_wave_rectifier","title":"Half-wave rectifier","text":"The diode only conducts on positive half-cycles (minus its 0.7 V drop), so the output is a train of humps. Click the switch to add a smoothing capacitor: the humps fill in, leaving ripple.","analysis":"tran","scope":{"tdiv":0.005,"v1":2,"v2":2,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[0,0]},{"ch":2,"at":[4,0]}],"sliders":[{"part":"C1","prop":"C","min":0.00001,"max":0.0005,"log":1,"label":"C"}],"parts":[{"type":"VAC","x":0,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"A":5,"f":60,"ph":0,"off":0},"name":"V1"},{"type":"D","x":0,"y":0,"p":{},"name":"D1"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"R1"},{"type":"SW","x":4,"y":0,"p":{"on":0},"name":"S1"},{"type":"C","x":8,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"C":0.0001},"name":"C1"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":4,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[0,4,8,4]]},
  {"id":"bridge_rectifier","title":"Full-wave bridge rectifier","text":"Four diodes steer both half-cycles the same way through the load, so the output has twice the ripple frequency. Probe 1 measures the source across its own terminals (a differential probe). Switch in the capacitor to smooth it.","analysis":"tran","scope":{"tdiv":0.005,"v1":2,"v2":2,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[4,0],"ref":[8,0]},{"ch":2,"at":[8,-4]}],"sliders":[{"part":"C1","prop":"C","min":0.00001,"max":0.0005,"log":1,"label":"C"}],"parts":[{"type":"VAC","x":4,"y":0,"p":{"A":5,"f":60,"ph":0,"off":0},"name":"V1"},{"type":"D","x":4,"y":0,"rot":3,"p":{},"name":"D1"},{"type":"D","x":4,"y":4,"rot":3,"p":{},"name":"D3"},{"type":"D","x":8,"y":0,"rot":3,"p":{},"name":"D2"},{"type":"D","x":8,"y":4,"rot":3,"p":{},"name":"D4"},{"type":"R","x":12,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"R1"},{"type":"SW","x":16,"y":-4,"rot":1,"p":{"on":0},"name":"S1"},{"type":"C","x":16,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"C":0.0001},"name":"C1"},{"type":"GND","x":12,"y":4,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[4,-4,12,-4],[12,-4,12,0],[4,4,12,4],[12,-4,16,-4],[12,4,16,4]]},
  {"id":"zener_regulator","title":"Zener voltage regulator","text":"The Zener diode clamps the output near 5.1 V while the input swings. Slide Vin from 8 V to 24 V: the output barely moves, because the extra current just flows through the Zener. Add load with RL.","analysis":"dc","sliders":[{"part":"V1","prop":"V","min":0,"max":24,"label":"Vin"},{"part":"RL","prop":"R","min":100,"max":5000,"log":1,"label":"Load RL"}],"parts":[{"type":"V","x":0,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"V":12},"name":"V1"},{"type":"R","x":0,"y":0,"p":{"R":220},"name":"R1"},{"type":"ZD","x":4,"y":4,"rot":3,"p":{"Vz":5.1},"name":"Z1"},{"type":"R","x":8,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":470},"name":"RL"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":4,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[4,0,8,0],[0,4,8,4]]},
  {"id":"led_circuit","title":"LED and current-limiting resistor","text":"An LED has a nearly fixed forward voltage (about 1.9 V for red), so without a series resistor the current is limited only by the supply. R sets I = (Vs - Vf)/R and the brightness. Try different values and LED colours (select the LED).","analysis":"dc","sliders":[{"part":"R1","prop":"R","min":47,"max":3000,"log":1,"label":"R"},{"part":"V1","prop":"V","min":0,"max":9,"label":"Supply"}],"parts":[{"type":"V","x":0,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"V":5},"name":"V1"},{"type":"R","x":0,"y":0,"p":{"R":330},"name":"R1"},{"type":"LED","x":4,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"color":"red"},"name":"LED1"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":4,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[0,4,4,4]]},
  {"id":"bjt_switch","title":"BJT as a switch","text":"A base current of about 0.9 mA through Rb drives the transistor hard into saturation (ten times what is needed), so about 9 mA flows through the LED. At 0 V the transistor is off and the LED is dark. Probe 2 is the collector voltage.","analysis":"tran","scope":{"tdiv":0.1,"v1":2,"v2":2,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[-6,6]},{"ch":2,"at":[8,8]}],"sliders":[{"part":"Rb","prop":"R","min":1000,"max":200000,"log":1,"label":"Rb"}],"parts":[{"type":"V","x":12,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"V":5},"name":"VCC"},{"type":"R","x":8,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":330},"name":"R1"},{"type":"LED","x":8,"y":4,"rot":1,"p":{"color":"green"},"name":"LED1"},{"type":"NPN","x":6,"y":8,"p":{"bf":100},"name":"Q1"},{"type":"GND","x":8,"y":12,"name":"GND"},{"type":"VP","x":-6,"y":6,"rot":1,"p":{"lo":0,"hi":5,"f":1,"duty":0.5,"td":0.25},"name":"V1"},{"type":"R","x":-6,"y":6,"p":{"R":4700},"name":"Rb"}],"wires":[[12,0,8,0],[8,12,12,12],[8,12,-6,12],[12,4,12,12],[-6,10,-6,12],[-2,6,-2,10],[-2,10,6,10]]},
  {"id":"common_emitter","title":"Common-emitter amplifier","text":"A voltage-divider-biased NPN amplifier with a bypassed emitter resistor. A 10 mV, 1 kHz input becomes a large inverted output (gain about -100). Probe 1 is the input, probe 2 the output; note the different volts/div.","analysis":"tran","scope":{"tdiv":0.0005,"v1":0.02,"v2":1,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[2,6]},{"ch":2,"at":[14,4]}],"bode":{"in":[2,6],"out":[14,4],"fmin":10,"fmax":1000000},"sliders":[{"part":"Re","prop":"R","min":200,"max":3000,"log":1,"label":"Re (DC bias)"}],"parts":[{"type":"V","x":18,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"V":12},"name":"VCC"},{"type":"R","x":6,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":47000},"name":"R1"},{"type":"R","x":6,"y":6,"rot":1,"p":{"R":10000},"name":"R2"},{"type":"NPN","x":8,"y":4,"p":{"bf":100},"name":"Q1"},{"type":"VAC","x":2,"y":6,"rot":1,"p":{"A":0.01,"f":1000,"ph":0,"off":0},"name":"Vin"},{"type":"C","x":2,"y":6,"p":{"C":0.00001},"name":"Cin"},{"type":"R","x":10,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":2200},"name":"Rc"},{"type":"R","x":10,"y":8,"rot":1,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"Re"},{"type":"C","x":12,"y":8,"rot":1,"p":{"C":0.0001},"name":"Ce"},{"type":"C","x":10,"y":4,"p":{"C":0.00001},"name":"Cout"},{"type":"R","x":14,"y":4,"rot":1,"p":{"R":10000},"name":"RL"},{"type":"GND","x":18,"y":16,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[6,0,18,0],[18,4,18,16],[6,4,6,6],[6,10,6,16],[6,6,8,6],[2,10,2,16],[10,12,10,16],[10,8,12,8],[10,12,12,12],[14,8,14,16],[2,16,18,16]]},
  {"id":"mosfet_switch","title":"MOSFET as a switch","text":"The gate draws no DC current: once Vgs exceeds the threshold (2 V) the channel conducts and lights the LED. At 0 V the channel is off. Probe 2 is the drain voltage.","analysis":"tran","scope":{"tdiv":0.1,"v1":2,"v2":2,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[-6,6]},{"ch":2,"at":[8,8]}],"sliders":[{"part":"Q1","prop":"Vt","min":0.5,"max":4.5,"label":"Threshold Vt"}],"parts":[{"type":"V","x":12,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"V":5},"name":"VCC"},{"type":"R","x":8,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"R":330},"name":"R1"},{"type":"LED","x":8,"y":4,"rot":1,"p":{"color":"green"},"name":"LED1"},{"type":"NMOS","x":6,"y":8,"p":{"Vt":2,"kp":0.05,"lam":0.02},"name":"Q1"},{"type":"GND","x":8,"y":12,"name":"GND"},{"type":"VP","x":-6,"y":6,"rot":1,"p":{"lo":0,"hi":5,"f":1,"duty":0.5,"td":0.25},"name":"V1"}],"wires":[[12,0,8,0],[8,12,12,12],[8,12,-6,12],[12,4,12,12],[-6,10,-6,12],[-6,6,-6,6],[-6,6,-2,6],[-2,6,-2,10],[-2,10,6,10]]},
  {"id":"cmos_inverter","title":"CMOS inverter","text":"A p-MOS pulls the output up when the input is low, an n-MOS pulls it down when the input is high. Drag the input slider: the output swings from 5 V to 0 V sharply near 2.5 V, and almost no current flows except while switching.","analysis":"dc","explainNode":[6,4],"sliders":[{"part":"Vin","prop":"V","min":0,"max":5,"label":"Input"}],"parts":[{"type":"PMOS","x":4,"y":0,"p":{"Vt":1,"kp":0.02,"lam":0.02},"name":"MP"},{"type":"NMOS","x":4,"y":4,"p":{"Vt":1,"kp":0.02,"lam":0.02},"name":"MN"},{"type":"V","x":0,"y":2,"rot":1,"p":{"V":0},"name":"Vin"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":8,"name":"GND"},{"type":"V","x":10,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"V":5},"name":"VDD"},{"type":"C","x":8,"y":4,"rot":1,"p":{"C":1e-12},"name":"CL"}],"wires":[[4,2,4,6],[0,2,4,2],[0,6,0,8],[6,0,10,0],[10,4,10,8],[0,8,10,8],[6,8,6,8],[6,4,8,4]]},
  {"id":"inverting_amp","title":"Inverting amplifier","text":"With negative feedback the inverting input is a \"virtual ground\", so the gain is simply -Rf/Rin = -10 and the output is upside-down. Increase the input or Rf until the output clips at the supply rails.","analysis":"tran","scope":{"tdiv":0.0002,"v1":1,"v2":5,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[-4,1]},{"ch":2,"at":[12,2]}],"bode":{"in":[-4,1],"out":[12,2],"fmin":10,"fmax":1000000},"sliders":[{"part":"Rf","prop":"R","min":1000,"max":30000,"log":1,"label":"Rf"},{"part":"V1","prop":"A","min":0.05,"max":2,"label":"Input amplitude"}],"parts":[{"type":"OA","x":6,"y":0,"p":{"vhi":12,"vlo":-12},"name":"U1"},{"type":"VAC","x":-4,"y":1,"rot":1,"p":{"A":0.5,"f":1000,"ph":0,"off":0},"name":"V1"},{"type":"R","x":-4,"y":1,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"Rin"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":-3,"p":{"R":10000},"name":"Rf"},{"type":"R","x":12,"y":2,"rot":1,"p":{"R":10000},"name":"RL"},{"type":"GND","x":12,"y":6,"name":"GND"},{"type":"GND","x":6,"y":3,"name":"GND"},{"type":"GND","x":-4,"y":5,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[0,1,6,1],[4,1,4,-3],[8,-3,12,-3],[12,-3,12,2],[10,2,12,2]]},
  {"id":"non_inverting_amp","title":"Non-inverting amplifier","text":"The input drives the + terminal and feedback through Rf and Rg sets the gain 1 + Rf/Rg = 11. The output is in phase with the input. Probe 1 is the input, probe 2 the output.","analysis":"tran","scope":{"tdiv":0.0002,"v1":0.2,"v2":2,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[2,7]},{"ch":2,"at":[12,2]}],"bode":{"in":[2,7],"out":[12,2],"fmin":10,"fmax":1000000},"sliders":[{"part":"Rf","prop":"R","min":1000,"max":30000,"log":1,"label":"Rf"}],"parts":[{"type":"OA","x":6,"y":0,"p":{"vhi":12,"vlo":-12},"name":"U1"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":1,"rot":1,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"Rg"},{"type":"GND","x":4,"y":5,"name":"GND"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":-3,"p":{"R":10000},"name":"Rf"},{"type":"R","x":12,"y":2,"rot":1,"p":{"R":10000},"name":"RL"},{"type":"GND","x":12,"y":6,"name":"GND"},{"type":"VAC","x":2,"y":7,"rot":1,"p":{"A":0.2,"f":1000,"ph":0,"off":0},"name":"V1"},{"type":"GND","x":2,"y":11,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[6,1,4,1],[4,1,4,-3],[8,-3,12,-3],[12,-3,12,2],[10,2,12,2],[6,3,6,7],[6,7,2,7]]},
  {"id":"summing_amp","title":"Summing amplifier","text":"An inverting op-amp adds its inputs: Vout = -(Rf/R1*V1 + Rf/R2*V2). Here V1 is a 1 kHz sine and V2 a DC level: slide V2 and the whole inverted sine shifts up and down (a level shifter / mixer).","analysis":"tran","scope":{"tdiv":0.0002,"v1":1,"v2":1,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[-2,3]},{"ch":2,"at":[16,2]}],"sliders":[{"part":"V2","prop":"V","min":-2,"max":2,"label":"V2 (DC)"},{"part":"V1","prop":"A","min":0,"max":2,"label":"V1 amplitude"}],"parts":[{"type":"OA","x":8,"y":0,"p":{"vhi":12,"vlo":-12},"name":"U1"},{"type":"R","x":2,"y":1,"p":{"R":10000},"name":"R1"},{"type":"R","x":2,"y":-3,"p":{"R":10000},"name":"R2"},{"type":"VAC","x":-2,"y":3,"rot":1,"p":{"A":0.5,"f":1000,"ph":0,"off":0},"name":"V1"},{"type":"GND","x":-2,"y":7,"name":"GND"},{"type":"V","x":-2,"y":-5,"rot":1,"p":{"V":1},"name":"V2"},{"type":"GND","x":-2,"y":-1,"rot":2,"name":"GND"},{"type":"R","x":8,"y":-5,"p":{"R":10000},"name":"Rf"},{"type":"R","x":16,"y":2,"rot":1,"p":{"R":10000},"name":"RL"},{"type":"GND","x":16,"y":6,"name":"GND"},{"type":"GND","x":8,"y":3,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[6,1,8,1],[6,-3,6,1],[-2,3,0,3],[0,3,0,1],[0,1,2,1],[-2,-5,0,-5],[0,-5,0,-3],[0,-3,2,-3],[8,1,8,-5],[12,-5,16,-5],[16,-5,16,2],[12,2,16,2]]},
  {"id":"integrator","title":"Op-amp integrator","text":"A capacitor in the feedback path integrates the input: a square wave becomes a triangle wave (slope = -Vin/RC). The large resistor across the capacitor just stops DC drift.","analysis":"tran","scope":{"tdiv":0.0005,"v1":2,"v2":1,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[-4,1]},{"ch":2,"at":[12,2]}],"tran":{"uic":true},"sliders":[{"part":"C1","prop":"C","min":2e-8,"max":5e-7,"log":1,"label":"C"}],"parts":[{"type":"OA","x":6,"y":0,"p":{"vhi":12,"vlo":-12},"name":"U1"},{"type":"VP","x":-4,"y":1,"rot":1,"p":{"lo":-1,"hi":1,"f":1000,"duty":0.5,"td":0.00025},"name":"V1"},{"type":"R","x":-4,"y":1,"p":{"R":10000},"name":"Rin"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":-3,"p":{"R":1000000},"name":"Rf"},{"type":"C","x":4,"y":-6,"p":{"C":1e-7},"name":"C1"},{"type":"R","x":12,"y":2,"rot":1,"p":{"R":10000},"name":"RL"},{"type":"GND","x":12,"y":6,"name":"GND"},{"type":"GND","x":6,"y":3,"name":"GND"},{"type":"GND","x":-4,"y":5,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[0,1,6,1],[4,1,4,-6],[8,-3,8,-6],[8,-6,12,-6],[12,-6,12,2],[10,2,12,2]]},
  {"id":"differentiator","title":"Op-amp differentiator","text":"A capacitor at the input makes the output proportional to the rate of change of the input: a square wave becomes spikes at each edge (inverted). A sine would become a cosine, shifted by 90 degrees.","analysis":"tran","scope":{"tdiv":0.0005,"v1":2,"v2":2,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[-4,1]},{"ch":2,"at":[12,2]}],"tran":{"uic":true},"sliders":[{"part":"Rf","prop":"R","min":200,"max":5000,"log":1,"label":"Rf"}],"parts":[{"type":"OA","x":6,"y":0,"p":{"vhi":12,"vlo":-12},"name":"U1"},{"type":"VP","x":-4,"y":1,"rot":1,"p":{"lo":-2,"hi":2,"f":500,"duty":0.5,"td":0.0005},"name":"V1"},{"type":"C","x":-4,"y":1,"p":{"C":1e-8},"name":"C1"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":-3,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"Rf"},{"type":"R","x":12,"y":2,"rot":1,"p":{"R":10000},"name":"RL"},{"type":"GND","x":12,"y":6,"name":"GND"},{"type":"GND","x":6,"y":3,"name":"GND"},{"type":"GND","x":-4,"y":5,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[0,1,6,1],[4,1,4,-3],[8,-3,12,-3],[12,-3,12,2],[10,2,12,2]]},
  {"id":"comparator","title":"Comparator","text":"With no feedback the op-amp output slams to a rail depending on which input is higher. The output goes high whenever the sine is above the reference. Move the reference to change the duty cycle.","analysis":"tran","scope":{"tdiv":0.002,"v1":1,"v2":3,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[0,3]},{"ch":2,"at":[12,2]}],"sliders":[{"part":"Vref","prop":"V","min":-1.5,"max":1.5,"label":"Reference"}],"parts":[{"type":"OA","x":6,"y":0,"p":{"vhi":5,"vlo":-5},"name":"U1"},{"type":"VAC","x":0,"y":3,"rot":1,"p":{"A":1,"f":100,"ph":0,"off":0},"name":"V1"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":7,"name":"GND"},{"type":"V","x":0,"y":1,"rot":3,"p":{"V":0.3},"name":"Vref"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":-3,"rot":2,"name":"GND"},{"type":"R","x":12,"y":2,"rot":1,"p":{"R":10000},"name":"RL"},{"type":"GND","x":12,"y":6,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[0,3,6,3],[0,1,6,1],[10,2,12,2]]},
  {"id":"schmitt_trigger","title":"Schmitt trigger","text":"Positive feedback gives the comparator two thresholds (about +0.5 V and -0.5 V): the output flips high only when the input falls below the lower one and low when it rises above the upper one, ignoring small noise in between.","analysis":"tran","scope":{"tdiv":0.002,"v1":1,"v2":3,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[0,1]},{"ch":2,"at":[12,2]}],"sliders":[{"part":"R2","prop":"R","min":2000,"max":30000,"log":1,"label":"R2 (feedback)"}],"parts":[{"type":"OA","x":6,"y":0,"p":{"vhi":5,"vlo":-5},"name":"U1"},{"type":"VAC","x":0,"y":1,"rot":1,"p":{"A":1.5,"f":100,"ph":0,"off":0},"name":"V1"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":5,"name":"GND"},{"type":"R","x":2,"y":6,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"R1"},{"type":"GND","x":2,"y":6,"name":"GND"},{"type":"R","x":6,"y":6,"p":{"R":9000},"name":"R2"}],"wires":[[0,1,6,1],[6,3,6,6],[10,2,12,2],[12,2,12,6],[12,6,10,6]]},
  {"id":"wien_oscillator","title":"Wien-bridge oscillator","text":"A Wien network (R and C in series and in parallel) passes exactly 1/3 of the output at f = 1/(2 pi R C) = 995 Hz with zero phase. The amplifier gain a little above 3 makes the oscillation grow from a tiny seed until the diodes limit it. Watch it start.","analysis":"tran","scope":{"tdiv":0.001,"v1":4,"v2":4,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[14,2]},{"ch":2,"at":[6,3]}],"tran":{"uic":true,"seed":true},"sliders":[{"part":"Rb","prop":"R","min":8000,"max":20000,"label":"Rb (gain trim)"}],"parts":[{"type":"OA","x":8,"y":0,"p":{"vhi":12,"vlo":-12},"name":"U1"},{"type":"R","x":14,"y":8,"rot":2,"p":{"R":10000},"name":"Rs"},{"type":"C","x":10,"y":8,"rot":2,"p":{"C":1.6e-8,"ic":0.3},"name":"Cs"},{"type":"R","x":6,"y":8,"rot":1,"p":{"R":10000},"name":"Rp"},{"type":"C","x":4,"y":8,"rot":1,"p":{"C":1.6e-8},"name":"Cp"},{"type":"GND","x":6,"y":12,"name":"GND"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":1,"rot":1,"p":{"R":10000},"name":"Rg"},{"type":"GND","x":4,"y":5,"name":"GND"},{"type":"R","x":8,"y":-3,"p":{"R":10000},"name":"Ra"},{"type":"R","x":12,"y":-3,"p":{"R":12000},"name":"Rb"},{"type":"D","x":12,"y":-6,"p":{},"name":"D1"},{"type":"D","x":16,"y":-9,"rot":2,"p":{},"name":"D2"}],"wires":[[12,2,14,2],[14,2,14,8],[6,8,6,3],[6,3,8,3],[6,8,4,8],[4,12,6,12],[8,1,4,1],[8,1,8,-3],[12,-3,12,-9],[16,-3,16,-9],[16,-3,18,-3],[18,-3,18,2],[18,2,14,2]]},
  {"id":"rc_ladder","title":"RC ladder (delay line)","text":"Three RC stages in cascade: each stage loads the previous one, so the output is a smoothed, delayed copy of the input. Probe 2 (the last node) lags probe 1 and its edges are rounded much more than a single RC.","analysis":"tran","scope":{"tdiv":0.001,"v1":2,"v2":2,"trig":0},"probes":[{"ch":1,"at":[0,0]},{"ch":2,"at":[12,0]}],"sliders":[{"part":"R1","prop":"R","min":200,"max":5000,"log":1,"label":"R (all stages)"}],"parts":[{"type":"VP","x":0,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"lo":0,"hi":5,"f":100,"duty":0.5,"td":0.001},"name":"V1"},{"type":"R","x":0,"y":0,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"R1"},{"type":"C","x":4,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"C":1e-7},"name":"C1"},{"type":"R","x":4,"y":0,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"R2"},{"type":"C","x":8,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"C":1e-7},"name":"C2"},{"type":"R","x":8,"y":0,"p":{"R":1000},"name":"R3"},{"type":"C","x":12,"y":0,"rot":1,"p":{"C":1e-7},"name":"C3"},{"type":"GND","x":0,"y":4,"name":"GND"}],"wires":[[0,4,12,4]]}
]
